      "Anda Cook, Class of 2022"
    ]
  },
  "summary": {
    "en": [
      "Anda Cook was born in Riga, capitol of Latvia, but when she was 9 years old, left with family to escape the advancing Soviet army. The family expected to return back home after the war, but it was not to be. Seven years were spent in Germany, first escaping heavy bombing, and after the war, a multitude of Displaced Persons` camps. After intensive screening and tests, Anda and family were allowed to come to the United States, arriving in 1952. The family`s sponsor was in South Dakota, so the first residence in the US was in Sioux Falls of that state."
    ]
  },
